    "exerciseText": "The artist is the creator of beautiful things. To reveal art and conceal the artist is art's aim. The critic is he who can translate into another manner or a new material his impression of beautiful things. The highest as the lowest form of criticism is a mode of autobiography. When I wrote the following pages, or rather the bulk of them, I lived alone, in the woods, a mile from any neighbor, in a house which I had built myself, on the shore of Walden Pond, in Concord, Massachusetts, and earned my living by the labor of my hands only. I lived there two years and two months. I went down yesterday to the Piraeus with Glaucon the son of Ariston, that I might offer up my prayers to the goddess; and also because I wanted to see in what manner they would celebrate the festival, which was a new thing. I was delighted with the procession of the inhabitants. Grandmaster touch typing is the ultimate synthesis of mental tranquility, physical precision, and instantaneous neuromuscular reaction. When eighty-five words per minute flows without conscious effort, the machine disappears completely into pure intellectual expression. Grandmaster transcription record 15: sustained flow across classical prose.",
